# The split-parent cap FLOOR. Do not edit casually -- see caps.baseline.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `the_cap_ratchet_only_turns_down` guarded
# DEFAULT_MAX_LINES and MAX_CAP_EXCEPTIONS against caps.baseline, but the nine
# split-parent numbers lived ONLY in caps.baseline -- the same file a raiser
# edits. `split_parents_stay_facades` read the cap from there and checked only
# `lines > cap`, so a split-parent cap could be raised with nothing failing.
#
# VERIFIED on 2026-09-19: raising all nine at once left the entire suite GREEN.
# Rule 4.4 had the same defect Rule 4.1's ratchet was written to fix, and
# `plan/05` §0 names it -- a rule that is not enforced is a wish.
#
# HOW IT WORKS. caps.baseline may hold a cap LOWER than the value here (a
# ratchet turn, silent and encouraged). A HIGHER one fails until this file is
# edited in the same commit, which puts the increase in a diff a reviewer
# cannot miss. Same mechanism as caps.baseline itself, one level up.
#
# FORMAT: `<path> <value>`, `#` comments and blank lines ignored.

crates/cena-model/src/crit.rs 300
crates/cena-model/src/state.rs 550
crates/cena-protocol/src/frame.rs 500
crates/cena-protocol/src/parser.rs 500
crates/cena-protocol/src/tags.rs 400
crates/cena-protocol/src/text.rs 450
crates/cena-session/src/actor.rs 650
crates/cena-session/src/supervisor.rs 650

